plined approach—avoid emotional attachment to the stock—and be prepared to re-enter if macro conditions improve or if Apple demonstrates strategic adaptations.  Finally, learn from past mistakes by not overestimating a dominant company’s ability to outperform market saturation and economic headwinds indefinitely. Continuous due diligence and skepticism towards overly optimistic narratives are vital. Regularly reassess the macroeconomic environment, technological innovation, and competitive landscape to inform your risk management approach.  In sum, I recommend selling Apple now. The combination of saturation, competition, and macroeconomic risks makes it too precarious to hold a long position at this point.
