ecovery, reassess positions accordingly. 5. Learn from past over-optimistic positions—this reinforces the importance of balancing growth potential with structural risks to avoid overexposure to vulnerable stocks.  In sum, while Apple remains a strong company with strategic advantages, the current valuation and industry environment warrant a more cautious stance. Going forward, I will stay attentive to macroeconomic signals and shifts in competitive dynamics to refine my approach and avoid past pitfalls of overly optimistic bias.
